        "original_id": "7ec93be1-2ac4-5c1b-912b-662addd1d71a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ricky Rubio, Kobe Bryant\n- Organizations: Minnesota Timberwolves, Los Angeles Lakers, Utah Jazz, Joventut, FC Barcelona, National Basketball Association\n- Events: 2011–12 Minnesota Timberwolves season, Rubio ACL and lateral collateral ligament injury\n- Topics: Rookie of the Year Award, NBA draft rights, player contracts\n\nFacts:\n- On August 31, 2009, Joventut traded Ricky Rubio's rights to FC Barcelona, and on the following day Ricky Rubio signed a six-year contract with FC Barcelona.\n- The 2011–12 Minnesota Timberwolves season was the franchise's 23rd season in the National Basketball Association.\n- During the 2011–12 Minnesota Timberwolves season, Ricky Rubio made his NBA debut with the Minnesota Timberwolves and was a contender for the Rookie of the Year Award.\n- During a game against the Los Angeles Lakers, Ricky Rubio tore his ACL and lateral collateral ligament after colliding with Kobe Bryant, and the injury ended his season.\n- Ricky Rubio, born on October 21, 1990, is a Spanish professional basketball player for the Utah Jazz of the National Basketball Association.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
